482
00:27:20,341 --> 00:27:21,375
Did you puke?

483
00:27:24,546 --> 00:27:25,913
I'm pregnant.

484
00:27:27,748 --> 00:27:28,849
(chuckles)

485
00:27:29,750 --> 00:27:30,885
What?

486
00:27:31,018 --> 00:27:33,020
- (upbeat music playing)
- (whimpers)

487
00:27:35,956 --> 00:27:37,626
Now, ideally, you're going
for a Gruyere,

488
00:27:37,758 --> 00:27:39,093
a Fontina, a Taleggio,

489
00:27:39,226 --> 00:27:41,362
but in a pinch, you could use
Monterey Jack,

490
00:27:41,495 --> 00:27:45,032
- Colby Jack, Pepper Jack...
- (door slams open)

491
00:27:46,000 --> 00:27:47,569
We'll hold, I guess.

492
00:27:47,701 --> 00:27:50,938
And this is Emily.
She put GourMaybe on the map.

493
00:27:51,071 --> 00:27:52,940
Emily: It's really nice
to meet you guys.

494
00:27:53,073 --> 00:27:55,644
I'm, um, a huge fan
of the show.

495
00:27:55,776 --> 00:27:57,044
What are you making?

496
00:27:57,178 --> 00:27:58,879
Emily: So, these are
crispy potato skins

497
00:27:59,013 --> 00:28:00,649
with a Cool Ranch Labneh dip.

498
00:28:00,781 --> 00:28:03,951
Yeah, we're doing a series
on elevated game day snacks.

499
00:28:04,418 --> 00:28:06,754
- Chelsea: Do you mind?
- Go for it.

500
00:28:10,525 --> 00:28:13,894
(munches) It's fun.

501
00:28:14,028 --> 00:28:15,996
You certainly don't skimp
on flavor.

502
00:28:16,497 --> 00:28:17,798
Zach: No, she doesn't.

503
00:28:19,133 --> 00:28:21,302
As someone who actually watches
a lot of sports,

504
00:28:21,435 --> 00:28:23,470
this assignment
came easily to me.

505
00:28:24,738 --> 00:28:27,041
And a guy's girl. I love it.

506
00:28:29,410 --> 00:28:30,311
(munches)

507
00:28:31,312 --> 00:28:32,647
(sighs) Psst.

508
00:28:33,047 --> 00:28:34,616
You sure
you wanna be caught talking

509
00:28:34,748 --> 00:28:37,785
- to some lowly dishwasher?
- Deena! Who are those people?

510
00:28:37,918 --> 00:28:40,287
Oh, the executive producers
of <i>The Boar.</i>

511
00:28:40,421 --> 00:28:42,456
I just watched
this talk they gave
at South By on YouTube.

512
00:28:42,591 --> 00:28:44,858
- They are total geniuses.
- It's effervescent.

513
00:28:44,992 --> 00:28:46,126
<i>The Boar?</i>

514
00:28:47,161 --> 00:28:48,563
You gotta be kidding me, Maddie.

515
00:28:48,829 --> 00:28:50,264
No, I'm not kidding you, Deena,
and you better tell me fast

516
00:28:50,397 --> 00:28:51,832
because they're coming over here
right now.

517
00:28:51,966 --> 00:28:53,100
Oh, <i>The Boar</i> is
about a restaurant,

518
00:28:53,234 --> 00:28:54,802
but really,
it's about so much more.

519
00:28:54,935 --> 00:28:56,705
It's also the hottest show
on TV right now.

520
00:28:56,837 --> 00:28:59,173
Oh, that's right.
You don't have a TV.

521
00:29:01,475 --> 00:29:03,844
Zach: And this is Maddie,
our newest chef,

522
00:29:03,978 --> 00:29:05,647
but already gaining
quite a following.

523
00:29:05,779 --> 00:29:06,880
Hi. (chuckles)

524
00:29:07,348 --> 00:29:08,949
Dan: And what do we have here?

525
00:29:09,083 --> 00:29:11,819
This is a Rotel dip,
but made with French techniques.

526
00:29:11,952 --> 00:29:13,454
How is that possible?

527
00:29:13,588 --> 00:29:16,390
Well, instead of using Velveeta,
I start with the béchamel,

528
00:29:16,524 --> 00:29:18,859
and slowly incorporate
quality cheeses.

529
00:29:19,326 --> 00:29:24,832
(munches) Damn. She's good.

530
00:29:25,600 --> 00:29:26,900
And her dip's good too.

531
00:29:29,504 --> 00:29:30,404
(slurps)

532
00:29:32,072 --> 00:29:33,173
What the hell was that?

533
00:29:33,608 --> 00:29:36,578
Oh, sorry, Maddie,
what the "heck" was that?

534
00:29:36,711 --> 00:29:38,513
Sit down. Let me explain.

535
00:29:39,547 --> 00:29:41,750
<i>The Boar</i> is looking to hire
their new culinary producer

536
00:29:41,882 --> 00:29:43,083
for their sixth season.

537
00:29:43,217 --> 00:29:44,719
And Disney wants FX
to pull somebody

538
00:29:44,852 --> 00:29:45,919
from the Condé Nast talent pool.

539
00:29:46,053 --> 00:29:47,522
Culinary producer?

540
00:29:47,656 --> 00:29:49,758
They need a new chef
to make a real menu

541
00:29:49,890 --> 00:29:51,825
for the fake restaurant
on the show.

542
00:29:51,959 --> 00:29:53,494
But they need somebody
with a vision.

543
00:29:53,628 --> 00:29:55,095
Somebody that's a star.

544
00:29:55,229 --> 00:29:57,231
They're gonna document
the whole thing with BTS content

545
00:29:57,364 --> 00:29:58,932
and pair that with each episode.

546
00:29:59,066 --> 00:30:02,169
But it's gonna be
very highbrow, cinematic AF,

547
00:30:02,303 --> 00:30:05,507
chef's table.
So, you know, be camera ready.

548
00:30:05,640 --> 00:30:07,074
So, it's down to us?

549
00:30:07,207 --> 00:30:08,475
Yeah, what about all the other
amazing chefs here?

550
00:30:08,610 --> 00:30:10,077
- Zach: I submitted you two...
- (grunts)

551
00:30:10,210 --> 00:30:11,879
...'cause you're
the two biggest stars I got.

552
00:30:12,647 --> 00:30:13,881
And admittedly...

553
00:30:15,316 --> 00:30:17,451
I like to watch you two
go at it.

554
00:30:17,585 --> 00:30:18,586
(clears throat)

555
00:30:20,187 --> 00:30:24,425
(dramatic music playing)

556
00:30:28,128 --> 00:30:32,132
- (door opening)
- (somber music playing)

557
00:30:39,873 --> 00:30:41,842
Someone's got
a little baby bump.

558
00:30:44,044 --> 00:30:45,179
- What?
- (chuckles)

559
00:30:45,613 --> 00:30:47,682
You're just a little fuller
in the tummy.

560
00:30:47,816 --> 00:30:49,116
It's beautiful.

561
00:30:50,652 --> 00:30:52,319
(kisses)

562
00:30:54,522 --> 00:30:56,123
Hey, I was thinking
we could pig out

563
00:30:56,256 --> 00:30:59,059
on something stanky tonight,
like Thai street food,

564
00:30:59,193 --> 00:31:01,195
and that new place
from Frogtown.

565
00:31:01,629 --> 00:31:02,963
(breathes deeply)

566
00:31:03,097 --> 00:31:05,065
We haven't really
celebrated yet, you know?

567
00:31:06,701 --> 00:31:08,902
- (kisses)
- Hmm.

568
00:31:09,470 --> 00:31:14,141
- (cutlery clinking)
- (indistinct chatter)

569
00:31:17,512 --> 00:31:19,246
Maddie, we'll be honest,
we're very excited about you.

570
00:31:19,380 --> 00:31:22,015
You have quite a few fans
over here at <i>The Boar.</i>

571
00:31:22,149 --> 00:31:23,518
We know
you're just starting out,

572
00:31:23,651 --> 00:31:25,787
but your food already has
a real identity.

573
00:31:25,919 --> 00:31:27,655
It's both youthful and timeless.

574
00:31:27,789 --> 00:31:29,624
It's full of verve,
but never pretentious.

575
00:31:29,758 --> 00:31:33,060
It sends a message,
and it tastes fucking good.

576
00:31:33,193 --> 00:31:35,797
Thank you, guys.
That... That really means a lot.

577
00:31:35,929 --> 00:31:38,232
We wanna know what your vision
for season six would be.

578
00:31:38,365 --> 00:31:39,667
Put together a presentation
of sorts,

579
00:31:39,801 --> 00:31:41,902
but take that
to mean whatever you want.

580
00:31:42,035 --> 00:31:45,472
Cook for us, take us out,
make a short film, a painting.

581
00:31:45,607 --> 00:31:46,574
We don't care.

582
00:31:46,708 --> 00:31:48,142
The important thing is
to tell a story.

583
00:31:48,275 --> 00:31:50,978
- (chuckles)
- What?

584
00:31:51,613 --> 00:31:54,148
It's just that
ever since I was a little girl,

585
00:31:54,281 --> 00:31:56,984
I always felt like cooking was
a form of storytelling.

586
00:31:58,051 --> 00:32:00,655
- You're speaking our language.
- Cool.

587
00:32:02,456 --> 00:32:04,224
Sorry to interrupt
the circle jerk,

588
00:32:04,358 --> 00:32:06,393
but did you guys get any word
from Disney on Maddie's chances?

589
00:32:06,528 --> 00:32:08,495
Well, they are
a little concerned

590
00:32:08,630 --> 00:32:11,231
- about her... stats.
- What do you mean?

591
00:32:11,365 --> 00:32:12,801
Your socials are weak.

592
00:32:12,933 --> 00:32:15,703
We need to beef up your presence
in the digital sphere.

593
00:32:15,837 --> 00:32:17,104
You have
some fierce competition.

594
00:32:17,237 --> 00:32:20,474
That's one word for her.
I... I... I mean, "it."

595
00:32:20,608 --> 00:32:23,578
(pensive music playing)

596
00:32:26,180 --> 00:32:28,750
- (upbeat music playing)
- Nina: Strong! Power!

597
00:32:29,249 --> 00:32:32,286
Confidence! Let's go!

598
00:32:33,053 --> 00:32:35,022
- Let's freestyle now.
- What?

599
00:32:35,155 --> 00:32:36,256
Nina: Step, step, hit and hit!

600
00:32:36,390 --> 00:32:38,025
Step, step, hit and hit!

601
00:32:38,158 --> 00:32:41,796
Your personality comes out here!

602
00:32:41,930 --> 00:32:43,130
Yeah, pump it, pump it.

603
00:32:43,263 --> 00:32:44,666
- You like that?
- Yeah, yeah.

604
00:32:44,799 --> 00:32:46,668
And pump, pump. Let's go! Pump!

605
00:32:47,334 --> 00:32:49,369
Pump, pump!
And whack it, and whack it!

606
00:32:49,504 --> 00:32:52,406
- Come on, Maddie, you baddie!
- Sorry.

607
00:32:53,974 --> 00:32:56,143
- Thank you guys so much!
- (all cheering, applauding)

608
00:32:56,276 --> 00:33:01,215
- Y'all hot right now?
- (all laughing)

609
00:33:01,348 --> 00:33:03,083
Maddie, remember,
it's not about getting it right,

610
00:33:03,217 --> 00:33:04,919
or being the best in class
all the time, girl.

611
00:33:05,052 --> 00:33:07,020
It's about letting the groove
move through your body,

612
00:33:07,154 --> 00:33:09,022
going with the flow,
and having fun.

613
00:33:09,156 --> 00:33:11,024
Groove and flow, got it. (pants)

614
00:33:11,158 --> 00:33:13,126
- You forgot fun, mama.
- (chuckles)

615
00:33:13,260 --> 00:33:14,729
Maddie, have you watched
<i>The Boar</i> yet?

616
00:33:14,863 --> 00:33:16,463
- Maddie: No.
- You can use my Hulu login.

617
00:33:16,598 --> 00:33:17,966
I don't care
if you know my password.

618
00:33:18,098 --> 00:33:19,634
Maddie: I haven't yet.

619
00:33:19,767 --> 00:33:21,468
I feel like I was just getting
my bearings at GourMaybe,

620
00:33:21,603 --> 00:33:23,303
and now I'm supposed
to fight like hell

621
00:33:23,437 --> 00:33:25,707
to be some food stylist
on a TV show?

622
00:33:25,840 --> 00:33:27,040
Oh, my God.

623
00:33:27,174 --> 00:33:28,308
Maddie, what they're doing
over there

624
00:33:28,442 --> 00:33:30,477
is so much more
than just food styling.

625
00:33:30,612 --> 00:33:33,515
Totally. It all sounds
so elevated and cool.

626
00:33:33,648 --> 00:33:35,382
I guess I just don't wanna get
my hopes up.

627
00:33:35,517 --> 00:33:37,351
Oh, you'll understand it
once you watch it.

628
00:33:37,484 --> 00:33:39,052
- Maddie: Uh-huh.
- We could binge it together.

629
00:33:39,186 --> 00:33:40,788
Aw, thanks,
but Jake would kill me

630
00:33:40,922 --> 00:33:42,991
if I didn't watch it with him.
He loves <i>The Boar.</i>

631
00:33:43,123 --> 00:33:45,225
Oh, right. Jake.

632
00:33:45,359 --> 00:33:47,629
- (pensive music playing)
- (door slams open)

633
00:33:48,563 --> 00:33:50,532
- Deena, are you okay?
- God.

634
00:33:50,665 --> 00:33:52,165
You know, Maddie,
since your promotion,

635
00:33:52,299 --> 00:33:53,635
it's like you don't have time
for me anymore.

636
00:33:53,768 --> 00:33:55,168
Like, you forgot about
all the little people.

637
00:33:55,302 --> 00:33:56,971
Deena... (scoffs)
...I didn't choose

638
00:33:57,104 --> 00:33:58,238
- any of this.
- (scoffs)

639
00:33:58,372 --> 00:33:59,473
Maddie: I feel
so out of control.

640
00:33:59,607 --> 00:34:00,875
Uh, it's all just happening
to me.

641
00:34:01,009 --> 00:34:02,242
Uh-huh. Sure about that?

642
00:34:02,744 --> 00:34:05,145
- What are you trying to say?
- It's funny.

643
00:34:05,279 --> 00:34:06,681
I really thought
we were best friends,

644
00:34:06,814 --> 00:34:08,983
but I guess you always saw me
as more of a coworker,

645
00:34:09,116 --> 00:34:12,554
- an occupational hazard.
- Of course we're friends.

646
00:34:13,086 --> 00:34:14,388
Deena, aren't you gonna
give me a ride?

647
00:34:14,522 --> 00:34:16,256
We always carpool
after dance class.

648
00:34:16,390 --> 00:34:17,926
- (engine revving)
- Deena: Yeah.

649
00:34:18,058 --> 00:34:20,028
Do you mind catching a lift?
You're kinda out of the way.

650
00:34:20,160 --> 00:34:24,431
- (engine revving)
- (gasps)

651
00:34:36,544 --> 00:34:39,047
- (screams, breathes heavily)
- Hey, hey, hey.

652
00:34:39,179 --> 00:34:40,480
It's just me.

653
00:34:40,615 --> 00:34:42,182
Jake, that was scary.
What are you doing?

654
00:34:42,316 --> 00:34:45,987
I know. I'm sorry.
I have a surprise for you.

655
00:34:46,119 --> 00:34:47,187
- Come on.
- Okay.

656
00:34:47,321 --> 00:34:50,123
(breathes heavily)

657
00:34:50,992 --> 00:34:52,159
I got you.

658
00:34:54,929 --> 00:34:55,863
Look.

659
00:34:57,164 --> 00:34:58,566
A buddy of mine from Middlebury

660
00:34:58,700 --> 00:35:01,435
makes these really dope replicas
of Amish furniture.

661
00:35:01,836 --> 00:35:04,539
He made this for his kid
and they don't need it anymore.

662
00:35:05,073 --> 00:35:06,406
Isn't it beautiful?

663
00:35:07,407 --> 00:35:10,912
It's... It's a little early.

664
00:35:11,646 --> 00:35:14,381
I'm sorry.
I guess I'm just excited.

665
00:35:14,949 --> 00:35:16,316
Am I the only one here that is?

666
00:35:16,450 --> 00:35:17,952
Maddie: Of course
I'm excited, Jake,

667
00:35:18,086 --> 00:35:19,754
but people normally wait
to get to the first trimester

668
00:35:19,887 --> 00:35:22,222
before they start making
these kinds of decisions.

669
00:35:22,356 --> 00:35:24,224
It could so easily go wrong,
you know?

670
00:35:24,358 --> 00:35:25,727
Jake: Why would you say that?

671
00:35:27,962 --> 00:35:29,296
- What is that?
- (sighs)

672
00:35:29,429 --> 00:35:30,698
I was gonna tell you.
Your mom signed us up

673
00:35:30,832 --> 00:35:32,600
for this monthly
frozen meat thing.

674
00:35:32,734 --> 00:35:35,202
- That bitch. (breathes shakily)
- I'll eat it, okay?

675
00:35:35,335 --> 00:35:37,105
Throw the steaks away
right now, Jake.

676
00:35:37,237 --> 00:35:38,740
But... (grunts)
...you're so passionate

677
00:35:38,873 --> 00:35:40,508
about reducing
food waste, Maddie.

678
00:35:40,642 --> 00:35:46,781
(breathes heavily)
I don't eat meat!

679
00:35:50,450 --> 00:35:52,386
Hi, guys. It's Maddie Ralph here

680
00:35:52,520 --> 00:35:54,388
in the sunny
GourMaybe Test Kitchen.

681
00:35:54,522 --> 00:35:56,924
Today, I am determined
to prove to you

682
00:35:57,058 --> 00:35:59,994
how much caramelization
you can get out of tofu.

683
00:36:00,128 --> 00:36:01,863
- Now, when people...
- (indistinct chatter)

684
00:36:01,996 --> 00:36:03,131
Kyle: Take your time.

685
00:36:03,263 --> 00:36:04,966
Kyle, why don't we, um,
start over?

686
00:36:05,465 --> 00:36:07,068
Okay, can everyone
please keep their work

687
00:36:07,200 --> 00:36:08,603
to a low hum?

688
00:36:08,870 --> 00:36:10,203
Maddie: Yeah, Kyle, it's fine.
We'll just take it again.

689
00:36:10,370 --> 00:36:11,338
Oh, my God,
I'm so fucking stupid.

690
00:36:11,471 --> 00:36:12,640
No, you're fine, Kyle.

691
00:36:12,774 --> 00:36:14,274
Were we being too loud
for you, Maddie?

692
00:36:14,809 --> 00:36:17,444
No, I actually wanted
to redo my intro anyway,

693
00:36:17,578 --> 00:36:20,313
so... (inhales deeply)
Hi, I'm Maddie.

694
00:36:20,447 --> 00:36:22,684
- Nice to meet you.
- Oh, I know who you are.

695
00:36:22,817 --> 00:36:25,687
My friends and I are obsessed
with your recipes.

696
00:36:25,820 --> 00:36:28,321
I'm Erin.
I'm the new you, I guess.

697
00:36:28,455 --> 00:36:30,024
Or the old you?

698
00:36:30,158 --> 00:36:31,626
- (laughs)
- (Erin laughs)

699
00:36:31,759 --> 00:36:33,928
Hi, Erin,
thank you for your kind words.

700
00:36:34,062 --> 00:36:35,830
Dishwashing can be
thankless sometimes,

701
00:36:35,963 --> 00:36:39,100
but remember that this company
could not exist without you.

702
00:36:39,232 --> 00:36:40,168
I would know.

703
00:36:40,300 --> 00:36:41,334
Erin: Thanks, Maddie. (chuckles)

704
00:36:41,969 --> 00:36:43,705
- I think we should...
- Sorry to overshare.

705
00:36:43,838 --> 00:36:45,338
- What's up?
- Erin: But...

706
00:36:45,472 --> 00:36:47,407
I used to have
a really disordered relationship

707
00:36:47,542 --> 00:36:49,777
to food. I mean, who doesn't?

708
00:36:51,713 --> 00:36:52,880
Totally.

709
00:36:53,114 --> 00:36:54,816
And I just have to say
it's really fucking refreshing

710
00:36:54,949 --> 00:36:57,185
to see a woman
with an actually healthy body

711
00:36:57,317 --> 00:36:58,953
making food content right now.

712
00:37:01,455 --> 00:37:02,824
What do you mean by "healthy"?

713
00:37:02,957 --> 00:37:06,594
You know, healthy, normal.
Like, not scary thin.

714
00:37:06,728 --> 00:37:08,930
- It's badass.
- (chuckles)

715
00:37:09,063 --> 00:37:10,832
(pot sizzling)

716
00:37:10,965 --> 00:37:13,968
Kyle, can we take lunch now?
I'll finish this later.

717
00:37:14,702 --> 00:37:17,739
- Okay.
- (pensive music playing)

718
00:37:19,540 --> 00:37:23,544
(breathes heavily)

719
00:37:24,879 --> 00:37:27,815
- (spits)
- What's the matter?

720
00:37:28,649 --> 00:37:30,151
Zach's spunk taste weird?

721
00:37:30,785 --> 00:37:33,955
- I wouldn't know.
- What's that supposed to mean?

