But then she added
one more step

1690
01:28:11,225 --> 01:28:13,060
to this endless cycle of hell.

1691
01:28:14,228 --> 01:28:16,363
She got a fake ID for me,

1692
01:28:16,496 --> 01:28:18,866
from a girlfriend of hers
in Oceanside...

1693
01:28:20,001 --> 01:28:21,836
and she took me to bars.

1694
01:28:23,638 --> 01:28:25,372
<i>The men would leer at me...</i>

1695
01:28:26,874 --> 01:28:29,342
<i>say disgusting things to me.</i>

1696
01:28:32,780 --> 01:28:34,649
And when they would touch me...

1697
01:28:35,683 --> 01:28:37,752
only then
would she step in. (sobbing)

1698
01:28:38,953 --> 01:28:41,756
But not because she wanted
to protect me.

1699
01:28:43,758 --> 01:28:45,893
She would take them
to the bathroom...

1700
01:28:47,995 --> 01:28:48,863
(cries)

1701
01:28:49,530 --> 01:28:51,464
...and finish them off.

1702
01:28:54,101 --> 01:28:58,072
She used me to procure men
for her... (sniffles)

1703
01:28:58,206 --> 01:29:00,975
...and told me it was
so I could have a father.

1704
01:29:01,976 --> 01:29:05,079
But I never needed
the love of a father.

1705
01:29:07,380 --> 01:29:09,317
I needed your love,
Mommy. (cries)

1706
01:29:10,117 --> 01:29:12,385
Careful, Maddie.
You're hurting my knee.

1707
01:29:18,826 --> 01:29:20,795
This is all I can do for today.

1708
01:29:26,067 --> 01:29:27,034
(door closing)

1709
01:29:28,336 --> 01:29:30,071
We're making progress, Maddie.

1710
01:29:31,072 --> 01:29:32,106
We're making progress.

1711
01:29:40,348 --> 01:29:42,016
(indistinct chatter)

1712
01:29:43,618 --> 01:29:45,119
(door closing)

1713
01:29:53,628 --> 01:29:56,030
- Hey, ladies.
- Patients: Hi, Nurse Hammond.

1714
01:29:56,163 --> 01:29:58,232
- (music concludes)
- Okay, we can all agree

1715
01:29:58,366 --> 01:30:00,368
that the food here sucks, right?

1716
01:30:00,500 --> 01:30:01,836
- Hmm.
- (chuckles)

1717
01:30:01,969 --> 01:30:03,638
Hammond: But I came up
with a brilliant idea.

1718
01:30:03,771 --> 01:30:06,741
How about Maddie
cook us lunch today?

1719
01:30:08,309 --> 01:30:09,810
(cheerful music playing)

1720
01:30:09,944 --> 01:30:11,579
Can I have help in the kitchen?

1721
01:30:11,712 --> 01:30:13,080
You sure can.

1722
01:30:17,251 --> 01:30:20,187
(inaudible)

1723
01:30:50,818 --> 01:30:52,653
You're the real deal, Maddie.

1724
01:30:55,523 --> 01:30:56,991
Can you pass the salad?

1725
01:30:58,125 --> 01:30:59,126
Thanks.

1726
01:31:01,796 --> 01:31:03,297
You really think I'm ready, Doc?

1727
01:31:03,731 --> 01:31:05,465
Only you can know that, Maddie.

1728
01:31:06,000 --> 01:31:07,034
Well, I do know

1729
01:31:07,168 --> 01:31:09,437
that I wanna get the hell
out of here.

1730
01:31:09,570 --> 01:31:10,871
(both chuckling)

1731
01:31:11,005 --> 01:31:12,506
Dr. Kronenfeld: Fair enough.

1732
01:31:13,407 --> 01:31:14,675
We're gonna miss you.

1733
01:31:15,810 --> 01:31:17,778
Hey, maybe I could come cook
for the patients again.

1734
01:31:17,912 --> 01:31:20,147
You know,
work with them in the kitchen.

1735
01:31:20,281 --> 01:31:21,415
We would love that.

1736
01:31:21,949 --> 01:31:23,985
But only if
that feels safe for you.

1737
01:31:29,724 --> 01:31:31,125
(footsteps fading)

1738
01:31:33,327 --> 01:31:34,628
She's ready.

1739
01:31:39,867 --> 01:31:41,635
Thank you both so much.

1740
01:31:42,103 --> 01:31:43,304
Bye now.

1741
01:31:43,437 --> 01:31:45,673
- We're so proud of you, Maddie.
- (Maddie chuckling)

1742
01:31:47,675 --> 01:31:48,843
(elevator bell dinging)

1743
01:31:52,980 --> 01:31:54,215
Maddie: Promise we'll see
each other

1744
01:31:54,348 --> 01:31:55,483
when you get out of here?

1745
01:31:55,616 --> 01:31:57,818
- Promise. (sobs)
- Maddie: Okay.

1746
01:31:59,587 --> 01:32:01,188
I'm going to miss you, guys.

1747
01:32:01,989 --> 01:32:03,357
I'm ready to go, too.

1748
01:32:03,491 --> 01:32:04,458
(music concludes)

1749
01:32:05,026 --> 01:32:06,927
- Deena, babe.
- Kelly: Deena.

1750
01:32:07,528 --> 01:32:08,963
This is Dr. Piggott

1751
01:32:09,096 --> 01:32:10,998
from the Behavioral Health
wing at Presbyterian.

1752
01:32:11,132 --> 01:32:12,500
She wants to ask you
a few questions

1753
01:32:12,633 --> 01:32:13,868
about your mental health
history.

1754
01:32:14,001 --> 01:32:15,903
We can't help you here,
and you know that.

1755
01:32:16,037 --> 01:32:19,140
I don't need any help.
No, Maddie can vouch for me.

1756
01:32:21,942 --> 01:32:23,310
You got this, Deena.

1757
01:32:24,779 --> 01:32:26,914
You're the toughest person
I know.

1758
01:32:27,882 --> 01:32:30,184
(sentimental music playing)

1759
01:32:31,952 --> 01:32:33,187
Maddie!

1760
01:32:34,055 --> 01:32:35,589
I'll see you in dance class?

1761
01:32:45,534 --> 01:32:47,034
(glass thudding)

1762
01:32:49,270 --> 01:32:50,204
Maddie!

1763
01:32:53,174 --> 01:32:54,942
- (glass thudding)
- Maddie!

1764
01:32:55,643 --> 01:32:58,245
Maddie! Maddie!

1765
01:33:01,215 --> 01:33:02,216
(music concludes)

1766
01:33:07,888 --> 01:33:09,090
Maddie: Mm.

1767
01:33:10,057 --> 01:33:11,926
Fig and Mortar, my favorite.

1768
01:33:12,626 --> 01:33:15,062
- Thank you so much.
- Of course.

1769
01:33:28,075 --> 01:33:30,744
You're allowed to be angry
with me, Jake.

1770
01:33:39,554 --> 01:33:41,155
(sighs heavily)

1771
01:33:48,563 --> 01:33:50,030
(chews)

1772
01:33:52,601 --> 01:33:53,901
I'm gonna go to the bathroom.

1773
01:33:59,907 --> 01:34:01,876
(door opening, closing)

1774
01:34:02,910 --> 01:34:06,113
(Maddie singing indistinctly)

1775
01:34:11,620 --> 01:34:12,953
(doorbell ringing)

1776
01:34:13,588 --> 01:34:14,822
(door creaks)

1777
01:34:16,991 --> 01:34:19,126
Hi. Is Maddie here?

1778
01:34:19,760 --> 01:34:21,195
Why?

1779
01:34:21,395 --> 01:34:23,397
I have something for her.
I could just leave it with you.

1780
01:34:23,864 --> 01:34:25,099
Jake, it's okay.

1781
01:34:30,004 --> 01:34:32,574
- Hi, Emily.
- Hi, Maddie.

1782
01:34:32,706 --> 01:34:33,908
Congratulations on <i>The Boar.</i>

1783
01:34:34,041 --> 01:34:35,776
They're really lucky
to have you.

1784
01:34:35,910 --> 01:34:37,745
Yeah, I got that one
fair and square.

1785
01:34:37,878 --> 01:34:39,146
(softly chuckles)

1786
01:34:39,280 --> 01:34:41,315
You think you'll come back
to GourMaybe?

1787
01:34:43,317 --> 01:34:45,386
I don't know
what I want anymore.

1788
01:34:46,053 --> 01:34:48,289
I'm certainly not ready
to see Zach.

1789
01:34:49,056 --> 01:34:50,191
Emily: He's gone.

1790
01:34:50,625 --> 01:34:53,961
<i>Condé Nast</i> found out
about our involvement.

1791
01:34:55,129 --> 01:34:56,030
Wow.

1792
01:34:57,231 --> 01:34:59,833
I made you tahini
chocolate chip cookies.

1793
01:35:02,203 --> 01:35:04,872
Bringing you food
was maybe weird, sorry.

1794
01:35:05,005 --> 01:35:07,074
No, it's really kind of you.

1795
01:35:08,042 --> 01:35:10,044
You know, I used to make
this recipe all the time

1796
01:35:10,177 --> 01:35:11,979
before I worked at GourMaybe.

1797
01:35:12,581 --> 01:35:13,582
I was a big fan.

1798
01:35:14,048 --> 01:35:15,684
Well, you know what they say.

1799
01:35:15,816 --> 01:35:17,218
Never meet your heroes.

1800
01:35:17,351 --> 01:35:19,420
They might be a giant cunt
to you for no reason.

1801
01:35:19,554 --> 01:35:22,089
- (chuckles)
- I'll get out of your hair.

1802
01:35:24,758 --> 01:35:26,060
Hey, what changed?

1803
01:35:26,661 --> 01:35:28,229
Why so nice all of a sudden?

1804
01:35:30,097 --> 01:35:32,466
I guess I just needed
to know you weren't perfect.

1805
01:35:35,537 --> 01:35:36,937
(upbeat music playing)

1806
01:36:04,865 --> 01:36:05,766
Hey.

1807
01:36:06,300 --> 01:36:07,801
- Where are you going?
- (music concludes)

1808
01:36:07,935 --> 01:36:09,136
Out for a run.

1809
01:36:10,538 --> 01:36:13,240
The doctor said it was okay
to exercise again?

1810
01:36:16,544 --> 01:36:17,444
Yes.

1811
01:36:20,147 --> 01:36:22,383
How do I know
you're telling me the truth?

1812
01:36:48,543 --> 01:36:49,843
(upbeat music playing)

1813
01:36:51,478 --> 01:36:52,479
(car trunk closing)

1814
01:36:59,853 --> 01:37:01,055
(sighs)

1815
01:37:05,492 --> 01:37:07,394
(upbeat music continues)

1816
01:38:03,718 --> 01:38:05,052
(music concludes)

1817
01:38:08,122 --> 01:38:10,290
♪ ("Only A Love"
by Michael A. Hesslein
playing) ♪

1818
01:38:29,977 --> 01:38:32,680
<i>♪ Only a little dream ♪</i>

1819
01:38:37,117 --> 01:38:42,389
<i>♪ To turn the world around us ♪</i>

1820
01:38:44,992 --> 01:38:48,128
<i>♪ Only a dream ♪</i>

1821
01:38:51,833 --> 01:38:57,237
<i>♪ To find what's left</i>
<i>That binds us ♪</i>

1822
01:38:59,440 --> 01:39:02,677
<i>♪ It won't be long now ♪</i>

1823
01:39:03,277 --> 01:39:07,649
<i>♪ It's like a song beginning ♪</i>

1824
01:39:08,382 --> 01:39:13,487
<i>♪ Reaching aloud to see ♪</i>

1825
01:39:13,822 --> 01:39:21,195
<i>♪ If only a love</i>
<i>Can take us there ♪</i>

1826
01:39:22,463 --> 01:39:25,065
<i>♪ Only a little love ♪</i>

1827
01:39:28,536 --> 01:39:33,875
<i>♪ If only a love can make it ♪</i>

1828
01:39:34,208 --> 01:39:38,011
<i>♪ To last the ages ♪</i>

1829
01:39:38,212 --> 01:39:43,984
<i>♪ Only you and me ♪</i>

1830
01:39:47,822 --> 01:39:52,292
<i>♪ Only a love ♪</i>

1831
01:39:52,694 --> 01:39:55,295
<i>♪ Only a love ♪</i>

1832
01:39:58,499 --> 01:40:01,301
<i>♪ If only a love ♪</i>

1833
01:40:01,502 --> 01:40:08,643
<i>♪ Can take us there ♪</i>

1834
01:40:21,990 --> 01:40:23,457
(song concludes)